h output during his time at the University of Cape Town is a testament to his intellectual prowess."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2533, "end": 2735, "text": "His publications, presentations, and collaborations with fellow scholars demonstrate a deep understanding of his field, as well as a commitment to advancing knowledge and addressing real-world problems."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 230, "text": "As David H Maphisa sat in the dimly lit café, surrounded by the aroma of freshly brewed coffee and the soft hum of intellectual chatter, he couldn't help but reminisce about his time at the Pontifical Catholic University of Chile."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 231, "end": 394, "text": "It was a place where the Andes Mountains met the vibrant streets of Santiago, where the air was alive with the whispers of revolution and the pursuit of knowledge."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 395, "end": 600, "text": "David's eyes wandered to the worn leather journal lying open on the table, its pages filled with notes and sketches from his research on the intersection of social justice and environmental sustainability."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 601, "end": 734, "text": "He had spent countless hours pouring over texts, attending seminars, and engaging in heated debates with his peers at the university."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 735, "end": 902, "text": "The Pontifical Catholic University of Chile had been more than just an institution – it was a crucible where his passions were forged, and his convictions were tested."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 903, "end": 984, "text": "As he sipped his coffee, David's mind drifted back to his favorite professor, Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 985, "end": 1092, "text": "Sofia Morales, who had challenged him to think critically about the role of faith in shaping social policy."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1093, "end": 1272, "text": "Her classes had been a masterclass in intellectual curiosity, where the boundaries between theology and sociology blurred, and the students were encouraged to question everything."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1273, "end": 1393, "text": "David's thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of his friend, Carlos, who slid into the booth with a mischievous grin."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1394, "end": 1447, "text": "\"Hey, David, I heard you're working on a new project."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1448, "end": 1511, "text": "Something about sustainable agriculture in the Atacama Desert?\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1512, "end": 1637, "text": "David nodded, and Carlos continued, \"I've got some connections with a local cooperative that might be willing to collaborate."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1638, "end": 1684, "text": "We should grab lunch and discuss the details.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1685, "end": 1845, "text": "As they chatted, David couldn't help but think about the ways in which his time at the Pontifical Catholic University of Chile had prepared him for this moment."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1846, "end": 2070, "text": "The university's emphasis on social responsibility, its commitment to fostering a sense of community, and its encouragement of interdisciplinary approaches had all contributed to his growth as a researcher and an individual."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2071, "end": 2176, "text": "The café's door swung open, and a group of students from the university walked in, laughing and chatting."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2177, "end": 2298, "text": "David's eyes met those of a young woman, her dark hair tied back in a ponytail, her eyes shining with a sense of purpose."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2299, "end": 2471, "text": "For a moment, they just stared at each other, two strangers connected by a shared experience, a shared passion for learning, and a shared commitment to making a difference."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "University of Cape Town", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Pontifical Catholic University of Chile", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "David H Maphisa", "scope": "educational institution attended", "claim": "David H Maphisa attended the University of Cape Town.", "answer": "University of Cape Town", "quote": "Born and raised in South Africa, Maphisa's innate curiosity and thirst for knowledge led him to pursue higher education at the University of Cape Town.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "David H Maphisa", "scope": "education", "claim": "David H Maphisa attended the Pontifical Catholic University of Chile.", "answer": "Pontifical Catholic University of Chile", "quote": "As David H Maphisa sat in the dimly lit café, surrounded by the aroma of freshly brewed coffee and the soft hum of intellectual chatter, he couldn't help but reminisce about his time at the Pontifical Catholic University of Chile. It was a place where the Andes Mountains met the vibrant streets of Santiago, where the air was alive with the whispers of revolution and the pursuit of knowledge. David's eyes wandered to the worn leather journal lying open on the table, its pages filled with notes and sketches from his research on the intersection of social justice and environmental sustainability. He had spent countless hours pouring over texts, attending seminars, and engaging in heated debates with his peers at the university. The Pontifical Catholic University of Chile had been more than just an institution – it was a crucible where his passions were forged, and his convictions were tested. As he sipped his coffee, David's mind drifted back to his favorite professor, Dr. Sofia Morales, who had challenged him to think critically about the role of faith in shaping social policy. Her classes had been a masterclass in intellectual curiosity, where the boundaries between theology and sociology blurred, and the students were encouraged to question everything. David's thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of his friend, Carlos, who slid into the booth with a mischievous grin. \"Hey, David, I heard you're working on a new project. Something about sustainable agriculture in the Atacama Desert?\" David nodded, and Carlos continued, \"I've got some connections with a local cooperative that might be willing to collaborate. We should grab lunch and discuss the details.\" As they chatted, David couldn't help but think about the ways in which his time at the Pontifical Catholic University of Chile had prepared him for this moment.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["University of Cape Town", "Pontifical Catholic University of Chile"]}
